            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say where, why and who. (कठै, क्यूं, कुण.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कद",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कद — kad — \"when\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आप कद आवो हो? āp kad āvo ho? — When do you come?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कद (kad) asks when. Monier-Williams gives Sanskrit kadā, \"when?\", but CDIAL has no entry for कद, so how the Marwari word came down is not settled. कदी, \"sometimes, ever\", opens the same way."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कद sits where the answer will go, as कठै does: वो कद जावै है? (vo kad jāvai hai?), when does he go?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
