          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ओळखणो",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ओळखणो — oḷakhṇo — \"to recognise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हूं यो गीत ओळखूं हूं। hū̃ yo gīt oḷakhū̃ hū̃. — I recognise this song."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आप यो गीत ओळखो हो? āp yo gīt oḷakho ho? — Do you recognise this song?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It opens on a letter you have not written yet: the vowel o, standing alone. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ओळखणो (oḷakhṇo) goes back to Sanskrit upalakṣayati, which CDIAL glosses \"beholds\". In that entry CDIAL gives Gujarati oḷakhvũ, \"to know, distinguish\", and no Marwari form (CDIAL 2226)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
