    {
      "id": "MW-W48-o",
      "sequence": 9800,
      "title": "ओ (o) — the letter that opens ओळखणो (oḷakhṇo)",
      "headword": "ओ",
      "romanization": "o",
      "gloss": "o — the letter that opens ओळखणो",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-type",
        "writing-block",
        "script-block",
        "eyes-or-hands-step"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:7bd29b175f808918",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [
          "a pen and something to write on",
          "your eyes, for letter shapes on the page",
          "your eyes or your hands for the steps that ask you to read, point, write or gesture"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Warm-up",
          "Script you'll notice: ओ",
          "Guided Practice",
          "Wrap-up Recall"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You will want a pen and something to write on, your eyes, for letter shapes on the page and your eyes or your hands for the steps that ask you to read, point, write or gesture. You can listen to everything else now. I will say so again when we reach them, but leave these sections until you have stopped: Warm-up, Script you'll notice: ओ, Guided Practice and Wrap-up Recall."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: write अ once, and name it. Then say छोरो (chhoro): its o is the sign ो."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now say ओळखणो (oḷakhṇo), \"to recognise\". It opens on the vowel o standing alone, and this lesson puts that letter in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: ओ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ओ — o."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It opens ओळखणो (oḷakhṇo). It is built on अ: the joined bowls, the shoulder and the inner stem, then a trailing stem, as आ has, and above it a separate arc, the same small arc the sign ो carries."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: ओ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "1. curve right around the upper bowl and continue down and around the lower bowl without lifting."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "2. lift and sweep the middle shoulder right."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "3. without lifting, climb up the inner stem to the headline."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "4. descend the inner stem."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "5. lift and descend the trailing stem."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "6. lift at the trailing stem's headline junction and sweep the upper arc upward and left."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "7. lift and draw the top shirorekhā left-to-right."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pen lifts: 4."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The source shows six movements; native writers draw ओ (o) as five pen-down strokes (60% of HP Labs India's native-writer samples, 49 of 82). This ductus follows the six movements in order and direction, lifting four times: the middle shoulder runs on, climbing the inner stem and descending it, and every other movement starts with a lift."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Stroke order is one attested teaching order; hands and teachers vary. Source: Saurmandal, ‘Devanagari ओ (o) stroke order.svg’, panels 1–6, Wikimedia Commons, 5 August 2023."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "at ओळखणो (oḷakhṇo) and point at ओ (o) at its start",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: at **ओळखणो** and point at ओ at its start]"
            },
            {
